  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8c5f8bea1b438d4687ad9b712e77c3e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level 1-5 After Battle Cutscene 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CutsceneData
  line:
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: They scared and lied to my mother as they would have any other mother.
      They threatened to condemn her if she did not say what they wished. She submitted
      to the will of her enemies and lost her spirit.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 3
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: The case became involved until the same alcalde asked pardon for her.
      But this was only when the matter was before the Supreme Court. He asked for
      the pardon because he was sorry for what he had done. Such was his meanness
      that I felt afraid of him.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 2
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: "Attorneys Francisco de Marcaida and Manuel Masigan, Manila\u2019s
      leading lawyers, defended my mother and they finally succeeded in having her
      acquitted. They proved her innocence to her judges, her accusers and her hosts
      of enemies. But how long did it take? After two and a half years? That is unacceptable."
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I found out for the first time what examinations were like. My examinations
      were in Christian doctrine, arithmetic and reading, in San Juan de Letran College.
      They gave me a passing mark and I returned to my home. A few days later came
      the celebration of the town festival, after which I went to Manila. But even
      then, I felt that unhappiness was in store for me.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Narrator
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: With Chapter III Complete. Let's start with the next chapter.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: 
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Chapter IV A Student in Manila
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
